{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/394464-thoughts-on-promethean-pride-and-the-refinement-phosphorus","id":394464,"title":"Thoughts on Promethean pride and the Refinement Phosphorus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-05T21:53:00-08:00","id":394464,"title":"Thoughts on Promethean pride and the Refinement Phosphorus","content":"Hey guys, I've been thinking about the game recently and a thought had occurred to me. What I think the reason why there's so much talk of transhumanism in this game is that there doesn't appear to be much PRIDE in being one of the Created. It's hard with wasteland and disquiet making life difficult, it's worse when the only good thing you can look forward to is NOT being what you are. Despite all the Supernatural advantages you may have.<br /> <br /> What I m enjoying about the upcoming 2nd (e) is that there are more ways to mitigate disquiet and the wasteland by taking on Roles. Still, not seeing the good that you already have takes a lot of the fun out of the game. Even the Refinement of Lead in the first edition made some mention that it's adherents made some small effort in finding the small joys of being one of the Created.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm excited to hear more about this new Refinement, Phosphorus. I mean think about it; every supernatural has a reason to get tot the top of their game power wise. If this can give one of the Created a good enough reason to revel in the fire they hold in their bodies, I'm all for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T22:18:50-08:00","id":394488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingme1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/394464-thoughts-on-promethean-pride-and-the-refinement-phosphorus#post394464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, I've been thinking about the game recently and a thought had occurred to me. What I think the reason why there's so much talk of transhumanism in this game is that there doesn't appear to be much PRIDE in being one of the Created. It's hard with wasteland and disquiet making life difficult, it's worse when the only good thing you can look forward to is NOT being what you are. Despite all the Supernatural advantages you may have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, every time I hear an argument like this, I find myself struggling against a knee-jerk reaction to characterize the poster as being only interested in the \u201ckewl powerz\u201d. <br /> <br /> No, Prometheans aren\u2019t so one-dimensional that the <i>only</i> good thing they look forward to is becoming human; it\u2019s \u201cmerely\u201d the <i>main</i> thing they look forward to. They <i>do</i> get to \u201cstop and smell the roses\u201d along the way; they just need to be careful not to become too complacent when doing so. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingme1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/394464-thoughts-on-promethean-pride-and-the-refinement-phosphorus#post394464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I m enjoying about the upcoming 2nd (e) is that there are more ways to mitigate disquiet and the wasteland by taking on Roles. Still, not seeing the good that you already have takes a lot of the fun out of the game. Even the Refinement of Lead in the first edition made some mention that it's adherents made some small effort in finding the small joys of being one of the Created.<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm excited to hear more about this new Refinement, Phosphorus. I mean think about it; every supernatural has a reason to get tot the top of their game power wise. If this can give one of the Created a good enough reason to revel in the fire they hold in their bodies, I'm all for it!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pilgrimage has that motivation built in, in that cranking your Azoth up to ten before you Redeem nets you benefits when you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T03:49:49-08:00","id":394648,"title":"","content":"When I'm running <b>Promethean</b>, I try to make sure to alternate plotlines about &quot;aggressively pursuing the Pilgrimage&quot; with &quot;weird, fun, supernatural shit.&quot; I also throw in, like, a block party now and again where people are just being nice to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T05:32:21-08:00","id":394700,"title":"","content":"I'd go to a Promethean-led block party. Sample the pot luck where Prommies have been experimenting with cooking. Teach one how to twerk, insisting that it's an important human cultural concept.<br /> <br /> Lots of fun to be had there. Until Disquiet sets in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T06:51:04-08:00","id":394742,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say that if you\u2019re teaching a Promethean how to twerk, Disquiet has <i>already</i> set in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T08:43:31-08:00","id":394935,"title":"","content":"Twerking is a universal milestone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T08:49:41-08:00","id":394941,"title":"","content":"Well, that's happening in my game now.<br /> <br /> Block part for a night sounds like an awesome way to start a game, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T21:49:54-08:00","id":395831,"title":"","content":"I see your argument. Let me go at this another way. I'm not trying to make the argument that the characters are one dimensional and that building up the Azoth and gaining &quot;kewl powers&quot; makes the game more interesting, what I'm trying to showcase is that the Pilgrimage, much like each character that walks it, is different. But for some,the desire to join the human herd might not be all that desirable. In fact,like Alchemy there is change and where one might see joining the masses bridges them closer to their goal, another perhaps after suffering so much abuse down through the years might see gaining morality a pointless gesture.<br /> <br /> This created sees only weakness, hostility, and the few mortals that know anything about the Divine Fire only want it to make themselves LESS human. Then the wheels begin to change. Better to gain power and rise above, screw the world and the pilgrimage. And thus you are now one of the hundred handed.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT . . . . And this is where I point out this new refinement,And much like The one rarified refinement where you do Alchemy for Alchemy's sake, THIS refinement has you glorifying your abilities and your &quot;superiority&quot; without loosing sight of the end goal. <br /> <br /> This is what a I'm talking about, not gaining powers but gaining POWER. And basking in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T22:02:55-08:00","id":395834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingme1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/394464-thoughts-on-promethean-pride-and-the-refinement-phosphorus?p=395831#post395831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your argument. Let me go at this another way. I'm not trying to make the argument that the characters are one dimensional and that building up the Azoth and gaining &quot;kewl powers&quot; makes the game more interesting, what I'm trying to showcase is that the Pilgrimage, much like each character that walks it, is different. But for some,the desire to join the human herd might not be all that desirable. In fact,like Alchemy there is change and where one might see joining the masses bridges them closer to their goal, another perhaps after suffering so much abuse down through the years might see gaining morality a pointless gesture.<br /> <br /> This created sees only weakness, hostility, and the few mortals that know anything about the Divine Fire only want it to make themselves LESS human. Then the wheels begin to change. Better to gain power and rise above, screw the world and the pilgrimage. And thus you are now one of the hundred handed.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT . . . . And this is where I point out this new refinement,And much like The one rarified refinement where you do Alchemy for Alchemy's sake, THIS refinement has you glorifying your abilities and your &quot;superiority&quot; without loosing sight of the end goal.<br /> <br /> This is what a I'm talking about, not gaining powers but gaining POWER. And basking in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not Phosphorum. Phosphorum's philosophy, as presented in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/its-complicated/\" target=\"_blank\">the blurb</a>, appears to be &quot;go for broke.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alchemy for alchemy's sake is <i>Mercurius</i>. &quot;Make yourself <i>less</i> human&quot; is <i>Centimanus.</i><br /> <br /> As Berg <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=383368#post383368\">notes</a>, Promethean existence means <i>you are on fire.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T22:28:56-08:00","id":395842,"title":"","content":"I appear to be missing something, because I\u2019m not seeing the distinction you\u2019re making between \u201cpower\u201d and \u201cpowers\u201d. It still seems to feature the same fallacy of looking at a Promethean\u2019s abilities as something to pursue for their own sake, rather than as useful tools to help get you through the Pilgrimage\u2019s hardships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T23:18:42-08:00","id":395866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingme1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/394464-thoughts-on-promethean-pride-and-the-refinement-phosphorus?p=395831#post395831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your argument. Let me go at this another way. I'm not trying to make the argument that the characters are one dimensional and that building up the Azoth and gaining &quot;kewl powers&quot; makes the game more interesting, what I'm trying to showcase is that the Pilgrimage, much like each character that walks it, is different. But for some,the desire to join the human herd might not be all that desirable. In fact,like Alchemy there is change and where one might see joining the masses bridges them closer to their goal, another perhaps after suffering so much abuse down through the years might see gaining morality a pointless gesture.<br /> <br /> This created sees only weakness, hostility, and the few mortals that know anything about the Divine Fire only want it to make themselves LESS human. Then the wheels begin to change. Better to gain power and rise above, screw the world and the pilgrimage. And thus you are now one of the hundred handed.<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT . . . . And this is where I point out this new refinement,And much like The one rarified refinement where you do Alchemy for Alchemy's sake, THIS refinement has you glorifying your abilities and your &quot;superiority&quot; without loosing sight of the end goal.<br /> <br /> This is what a I'm talking about, not gaining powers but gaining POWER. And basking in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Typical, &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transhumanism\" target=\"_blank\">transhuman</a>&quot; motivation of characters that are viable and still omitted by devs. On quick note I point to you that by now rules, all PCs must participate in Pilgirmage - in 2ed they can change Refiments and Roles. If they still will stahl, the Quashmallims will make them. Diversion from it is in Storyteller field as it's house rule, even if this question come up each time in few weeks interval, in various forms.<br /> <br /> As to playing this kind character, I advise Refinments of Argentum, Stannum and Plumbum. They all are connected to the idea of making Prometheans something other than humans, without making them monsters - like Centimani. And for more thoughts and ideas on the subject, I send you to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here\">Transhuman Promethean topic</a> on the forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T08:42:32-08:00","id":396396,"title":"","content":"Ah yes...this old argument again. <br /> <br /> Honestly why is it so hard for people to get behind the idea that being a Promethean is not a desirable state? (Particularly in the WoD where power always has horrible costs/risks) <br /> Why is it so hard for people to grasp the idea that being Human is a good thing? Or humanity can be awesome all by itself, despite our flaws and weaknesses? <br /> Really where is the love for the humanist ideals at the core of this game?<br /> <br /> Honestly, every time I see one of these threads I just want to plaster <b>&quot;Missing the Point&quot;</b> across my screen with a big ink stamp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T18:16:49-08:00","id":398270,"title":"","content":"Well, look at it another way this might not be so &quot;transhuman&quot; after all. If so many of US, PLAYERS - HUMANS - want to play characters that get some kewl neeto powaz, what does this say about the human life? We crave more, we always crave more - we want the easy way.<br /> <br /> Wanting power IS one of the most human of desires. Wanting it SO YOU'RE NO LONGER HUMAN might not be in point with the game though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T23:14:24-08:00","id":398471,"title":"","content":"First of all in terms of trans-humanism, with the current dependency that all of us have on technology, you could say that we might already be something trans-human. In regards to OPs concern with Prometheans having pride. The Promethean's understanding of what is real is clashing with what is objectively real, why take pride in that? Human society also has an objective reality as it is determined by humans collectively. It is the Promethean's acting against the way the real world of humans and nature works, that is causing the disquiet and wasteland. There is a real true reality that is beyond all of our opinions. Do I know what it is? Hell no! I only deduce that there does have to be <i>something</i> that is Real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4811-thinking_point","name":"Thinking_Point","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:44:22-07:00","id":432618,"title":"","content":"The thing is with Prometheans in general is not about them becoming human if they happen to have seen enough to have no faith in people, but more they want to fit in somewhere, even if the people around them aren't inherently nice to them before. Going outside of the flaws a Promethean has; Disquiet, Pandoran summoning, Torment, ease of gaining Derangements, others of their kind out to do lacuna for their Vitriol, Wasteland formation... They inherently don't fit in and that breeds loneliness, though more than that, people naturally react badly to them, mobs can form against them if their Azoth is strong enough... Some just aren't mentally capable or they end up that way through their wandering to defend themselves in a social manner, which causes more problems... Sure, they can boost up their Azoth to collect up more Pyros and gain loads of them Transmutations if they're adept to fight off the lynching and Pandoran attacks... They're hardy creatures and electricity heals them... But they'll always be lonely and even in a throng always know that they're 'different', 'inhuman' even. It must wear on them, to always be walking onwards, never being able to settle or find company that won't eventually go deranged on them from the Disquiet they exude... Poisoning the land around them into a Wasteland. It may not be ideal, but to fit in and find company, a loved one, to settle down, to not be hunted down by everything... These are things some humans may take for granted, but when you're unable to have these things that make life tolerable... Well perhaps having some superpower angst makes more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:14:35-07:00","id":432709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/394464-thoughts-on-promethean-pride-and-the-refinement-phosphorus?p=394648#post394648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I'm running <b>Promethean</b>, I try to make sure to alternate plotlines about &quot;aggressively pursuing the Pilgrimage&quot; with &quot;weird, fun, supernatural shit.&quot; I also throw in, like, a block party now and again where people are just being nice to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This reminds me of my long-running semi-serious intent to run a game of Promethean based around a throng competing in an amateur-league sport (any team sport, really) tournament. <br /> <br /> They're having to hide their supernatural powers, the other teams all hate them, the fouls against them go ignored by a hostile ref, the crowd boos them.. Can they take home the cup?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:24:45-07:00","id":432718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/394464-thoughts-on-promethean-pride-and-the-refinement-phosphorus?p=432709#post432709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me of my long-running semi-serious intent to run a game of Promethean based around a throng competing in an amateur-league sport (any team sport, really) tournament.<br /> <br /> They're having to hide their supernatural powers, the other teams all hate them, the fouls against them go ignored by a hostile ref, the crowd boos them.. Can they take home the cup?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 11/10<br /> Plot idea of the Forever.<br /> <br /> Dangit, man, you make me want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0